WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.636
Four independent trials
Toss a fair coin four times independently. X counts heads. We want the
probability of obtaining heads exactly twice.

2
00:00:11.636 --> 00:00:26.000
Check the binomial model
There are four trials, and the success probability in each is one half.
Independence and this constant probability allow us to use the binomial
distribution.

3
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:38.545
Choose the success positions
Choose which two of the four positions will contain successes. The number of
choices is four choose two, equal to six.

4
00:00:38.545 --> 00:00:51.545
Probability of each arrangement
Each arrangement with two successes and two failures has probability one half
squared times one half squared. The product is one sixteenth.

5
00:00:51.545 --> 00:01:03.636
Add the six cases
There are six distinct arrangements with the same probability. Multiply six by
one sixteenth and simplify to obtain three eighths.

6
00:01:03.636 --> 00:01:18.000
Exactly two successes
This is the probability of exactly two heads, not at least two. If the wording
changes, the events included in the calculation must also change.
